 potentially very  important here whatever you think about  Barack Obama or  Joe Biden a highly involved Barack Obama  improves the chances that Donald Trump  is defeated you might remember back in  2008 george w bush was very unpopular  and was almost completely missing from  the campaign trail in support of the  Republican nominee John McCain just  didn't make sense it was possibly going  to hurt John McCain to have George W  Bush heavily involved in the 2008  Republican campaign for the presidency  ultimately McCain lost anyway to Barack  Obama in this case it's very very  different if and when the the real  campaigning is able to get going and  this will depend on the virus of course  there may be a window there between you  know early July through late September  maybe before wave 2 is likely to hit  where there will be some real  campaigning I believe it's a very good  thing for Joe Biden for Barack Obama to  be right there with him and for better  or worse Obama there with Biden will  create the contrast in people's minds of  Trump versus what things were like under  Barack Obama now I want to be really  clear about what I mean by that Barack  Obama was wrong on many issues right the  Obama administration's dealing of with  whistleblowers was not good the Obama  administration's drone warfare policy  was not good we could go on and on but  the u.s. was respected as an adult was  leading us back then because we had an  adult leading us and with the country  shut down it's very difficult to gain  any momentum if you're Joe Biden Trump  is making bad decisions daily with  coronavirus but sadly many of his  followers seem to fall more and more in  love with Trump the worst his decisions  on coronavirus are some even see Trump  is decisive and strong and powerful in  the context of coronavirus so Biden  needs to do something to get attention  and start building momentum okay I guess  eventually there are going to be debates  we don't know exactly what the format  